<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Konstantin Konik</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1873">1873</a>–<a href="/years/1936">1936</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Konstantin Konik was an Estonian surgeon and politician. In February 1918 he was one of the three members of the Salvation Committee, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstantin-pats">Konstantin Päts</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juri-vilms">Jüri Vilms</a>, which issued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonian-declaration-of-independence">Manifesto to the Peoples of Estonia</a> proclaiming independence. A physician by profession, he remained active in the public life of the independent republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/konstantin-konik.jpg" alt="Konstantin Konik" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heinrich Riedel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Konstantin_Konik.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
